# Vercel Web Analytics Installation Report

## Summary
Successfully installed and configured Vercel Web Analytics for the Next.js project following the latest official documentation from https://vercel.com/docs/analytics/quickstart.

## Changes Made

### 1. Package Installation
- **Installed**: `@vercel/analytics` package (version installed via npm)
- **Package Manager**: npm
- **Lock File Updated**: `package-lock.json` updated with new dependencies

### 2. Code Changes
**Modified**: `frontend/src/app/layout.tsx`

Added the Analytics component to the root layout following Next.js App Router best practices:

1. **Import Statement**: Added `import { Analytics } from "@vercel/analytics/next";` at the top of the file
2. **Component Integration**: Added `<Analytics />` component inside the `<body>` tag, after the main content and BakeryProvider

The Analytics component is properly positioned at the end of the body to ensure optimal loading and tracking without affecting the user experience.

### 3. Implementation Details
- **Framework**: Next.js 16.3.0 with App Router
- **Location**: Root layout (`src/app/layout.tsx`)
- **Integration Method**: Framework-specific Next.js import (`@vercel/analytics/next`)
- **Placement**: End of body tag as recommended by Vercel documentation

### 4. Verification Steps Completed
✓ Package installed successfully using npm
✓ Build completed successfully with no errors
✓ TypeScript compilation passed
✓ All static pages generated correctly (19 routes)
✓ Linter run completed (no new errors introduced by Analytics integration)
✓ Lock file properly updated with new dependency

## Next Steps for Users
1. **Enable Analytics in Vercel Dashboard**: Navigate to your project's Analytics section in the Vercel dashboard and click "Enable" to activate Web Analytics
2. **Deploy**: Deploy the application to Vercel using `vercel deploy` or push to your connected git repository
3. **Verify**: After deployment, check the browser's Network tab for analytics requests to `/<unique-path>/view` to confirm tracking is working
4. **Monitor**: View analytics data in your Vercel project dashboard

## Implementation Notes
- The implementation strictly follows the official Vercel documentation retrieved on 2026-08-15
- Uses the framework-specific Next.js import for optimal performance
- Preserves all existing code structure and styling
- No breaking changes introduced
- Analytics component will be inert during local development and only active on Vercel-deployed environments
